From: N60 Pro platform integration
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: keep MT7986 WED under Logan WARP control

The MT7986 vendor WARP implementation registers its own platform drivers
for the Logan WED nodes.  Do not also pass those nodes to the upstream WED
attach path in the Ethernet driver: the MT7988 Logan-WARP DTS conversion
already removes this property for the same reason.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7986a.dtsi
@@ -611,7 +611,6 @@
 			mediatek,ethsys = <&ethsys>;
 			mediatek,sgmiisys = <&sgmiisys0>, <&sgmiisys1>;
 			mediatek,wed-pcie = <&wed_pcie>;
-			mediatek,wed = <&wed>, <&wed2>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
